---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Western MA school spending explorer - Tim Shores"
  description="Per-pupil spending, enrollment, and Chapter 70 aid for Western Massachusetts school districts, FY2009 to FY2025"
>
  <section id="explorer" class="explorer is-loading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Western Massachusetts · FY2009–FY<span data-latest>2025</span></p>
    <h1>School spending explorer</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Per-pupil spending, enrollment, and state aid for 65 Western Massachusetts school districts, from the
      data behind my report on
      <a href="/artifacts/western-ma-ppe-report.pdf">per-pupil expenditure in Western Massachusetts</a>.
    </p>

    <form class="controls" onsubmit="return false">
      <label class="control">
        <span>District</span>
        <select id="pick-district"></select>
      </label>
      <label class="control">
        <span>Compare with</span>
        <select id="pick-compare">
          <option value="cohort">Its cohort average</option>
          <option value="western">Western MA average</option>
          <option value="none">No comparison</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <fieldset class="control toggle">
        <legend>Dollars</legend>
        <div class="toggle-options">
          <label><input type="radio" name="dollars" value="nominal" checked /><span>Nominal</span></label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="dollars" value="real" /><span>FY<span data-latest>2025</span> dollars</span></label>
        </div>
      </fieldset>
    </form>

    <header class="entity">
      <h2 id="entity-name">Loading…</h2>
      <p id="entity-meta"></p>
    </header>

    <div id="tiles" class="tiles"></div>

    <div id="panels" class="panels">
      <figure id="fig-ppe" class="panel">
        <h3>Spending per pupil by category</h3>
        <p class="panel-sub" id="ppe-sub"></p>
        <ul class="legend" id="legend-ppe"></ul>
        <svg id="svg-ppe" tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="Stacked columns of spending per pupil by category for each fiscal year. Use the arrow keys to read each year; the data table below has every value."></svg>
        <div class="tooltip" role="status" hidden></div>
        <details class="table-view">
          <summary>Data table</summary>
          <div class="table-scroll" id="table-ppe"></div>
        </details>
      </figure>

      <figure id="fig-enroll" class="panel">
        <h3>Enrollment</h3>
        <p class="panel-sub" id="enroll-sub"></p>
        <ul class="legend" id="legend-enroll"></ul>
        <svg id="svg-enroll" tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="Lines of in-district, foundation, and out-of-district enrollment for each fiscal year. Use the arrow keys to read each year; the data table below has every value."></svg>
        <div class="tooltip" role="status" hidden></div>
        <details class="table-view">
          <summary>Data table</summary>
          <div class="table-scroll" id="table-enroll"></div>
        </details>
      </figure>

      <figure id="fig-nss" class="panel">
        <h3>Chapter 70 aid and net school spending</h3>
        <p class="panel-sub" id="nss-sub"></p>
        <ul class="legend" id="legend-nss"></ul>
        <svg id="svg-nss" tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="Stacked columns of Chapter 70 aid, required local contribution, and spending above the requirement per foundation pupil for each fiscal year. Use the arrow keys to read each year; the data table below has every value."></svg>
        <div class="tooltip" role="status" hidden></div>
        <details class="table-view">
          <summary>Data table</summary>
          <div class="table-scroll" id="table-nss"></div>
        </details>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <section class="notes">
      <h2>About the data</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Spending per pupil</strong> is the Massachusetts Department of Elementary and Secondary Education's
        (DESE) per-pupil expenditure from each district's end-of-year report, divided by in-district FTE and grouped
        into the report's nine categories. It leaves out tuition for pupils educated elsewhere, because, as DESE puts
        it, those costs "vary greatly depending on the reason for going out of district."
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Enrollment</strong> comes in three measures. In-district FTE is full-year enrollment of students who
        live in the district or are choiced or tuitioned into it. Foundation enrollment counts the residents the
        district is financially responsible for on October 1 of the prior year. Out-of-district FTE counts the
        district's pupils educated elsewhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Chapter 70 aid and net school spending</strong> are per foundation pupil. The state sets a required
        level of net school spending for each district each year. Chapter 70 aid pays part of it, and the town, or a
        regional district's member towns, pays the required local contribution. Anything above that is a local choice. Because spending per pupil and
        net school spending use different denominators, the two charts are not the same measure: they are a picture
        of apples in the morning compared with a picture of apples in the evening. Both dollar charts share one scale.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Cohorts</strong> group districts by FY<span data-latest>2025</span> in-district FTE, using the
        boundaries the report set from FY2024 enrollment: Tiny up to 200 FTE, Small 201–800, Medium 801–1,600, and
        Large 1,601–10,000. Springfield stands apart. Cohort and Western MA spending averages are weighted by
        in-district FTE, Chapter 70 averages by foundation enrollment, and enrollment averages are per district. The
        Western MA average covers the 64 districts other than Springfield.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>FY<span data-latest>2025</span> dollars</strong> adjust for inflation with the Bureau of Labor
        Statistics' consumer price index for the Northeast (CPI-U, series CUUR0100SA0), averaged over each July–June
        fiscal year.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Sources:</strong>
        <a href="https://educationtocareer.data.mass.gov/d/er3w-dyti">DESE District Expenditures by Spending Category</a>
        (Education-to-Career hub),
        <a href="https://www.doe.mass.edu/finance/chapter70/default.html">DESE Chapter 70 district profiles</a>, and
        <a href="https://data.bls.gov/timeseries/CUUR0100SA0">BLS CPI-U Northeast</a>. Built by Tim Shores with
        Claude Code. The code that prepares the data is at
        <a href="https://github.com/timshores/schools">github.com/timshores/schools</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script>
  import { startExplorer } from "../../lib/massppe/explorer";
  startExplorer();
</script>

<style>
  .explorer {
    --surface: var(--paper);
    --grid: #e9e3d7;
    --axis: #b9b1a2;
    --muted: #6d695e;
    font-variant-numeric: normal;
  }

  .explorer.is-loading .panels {
    opacity: 0.4;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  /* Controls: one row above everything they scope */
  .controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.4rem 0 1.6rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
  }

  .control {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    border: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .control select {
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  #pick-district {
    min-width: 15rem;
  }

  .toggle legend {
    padding: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .toggle-options {
    display: flex;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--paper);
  }

  .toggle-options label {
    position: relative;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .toggle-options input {
    position: absolute;
    opacity: 0;
    inset: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .toggle-options span {
    display: block;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .toggle-options span span {
    display: inline;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .toggle-options label + label {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .toggle-options input:checked + span {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .toggle-options input:checked + span span {
    background: none;
  }

  .toggle-options input:focus-visible + span {
    outline: 2px dashed var(--accent);
    outline-offset: -4px;
  }

  .entity h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
  }

  .entity p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  /* Stat tiles */
  .tiles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
  }

  .tiles :global(.tile) {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem;
  }

  .tiles :global(.tile-label) {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .tiles :global(.tile-value) {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0.15rem;
  }

  .tiles :global(.tile-detail) {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  /* Panels */
  .panels {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .panel {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .panel h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }

  .panel-sub {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legend {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.25rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .legend :global(li) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .panel :global(.key) {
    flex: none;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .panel :global(.key.rect) {
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--c);
  }

  .panel :global(.key.line) {
    width: 16px;
    height: 2px;
    border-radius: 1px;
    background: var(--c);
  }

  .panel :global(.key.hatch) {
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, var(--c) 0 1px, transparent 1px 4px);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--axis);
  }

  .panel :global(.key.none) {
    width: 16px;
  }

  .panel svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    overflow: visible;
    font-family: "Space Grotesk", sans-serif;
    touch-action: pan-y;
  }

  .panel svg:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px dashed var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 4px;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .panel :global(.gridline) {
    stroke: var(--grid);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .panel :global(.baseline) {
    stroke: var(--axis);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .panel :global(.tick) {
    font-size: 12px;
    fill: var(--muted);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .panel :global(.cap),
  .panel :global(.end-label) {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    fill: var(--ink-soft);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .panel :global(.band) {
    fill: var(--ink);
    opacity: 0.045;
  }

  .panel :global(.hit) {
    fill: transparent;
    cursor: crosshair;
  }

  .panel :global(.col) {
    transition: opacity 0.12s ease;
  }

  .panel :global(svg.has-hover .col:not(.is-hover)) {
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .panel :global(svg .col.faded),
  .panel :global(svg.has-hover .col.faded:not(.is-hover)) {
    opacity: 0.35;
  }

  .panel :global(.hatch-bg) {
    fill: var(--surface);
  }

  .panel :global(.hatch-line) {
    stroke: var(--ink-soft);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .panel :global(.overlay-line),
  .panel :global(.series-line) {
    fill: none;
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }

  .panel :global(.dot) {
    stroke: var(--surface);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }

  .panel :global(.crosshair) {
    stroke: var(--axis);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .panel :global(.hit),
  .panel :global(.overlay),
  .panel :global(.lines) {
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .panel :global(.hit) {
    pointer-events: all;
  }

  /* Tooltip: value first, label after, line keys */
  .tooltip {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    min-width: 13rem;
    max-width: min(25rem, calc(100% - 8px));
    padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 22px var(--shadow);
    pointer-events: none;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .tooltip :global(.tip-title) {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .tooltip :global(.tip-row) {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 16px auto 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .tooltip :global(.tip-value) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    text-align: right;
    min-width: 4.6rem;
  }

  .tooltip :global(.tip-label) {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .tooltip :global(.tip-row.strong) {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-bottom: 0.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }

  .tooltip :global(.tip-note) {
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* Table view */
  .table-view {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .table-view summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 500;
    width: max-content;
  }

  .table-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .table-scroll :global(table) {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .table-scroll :global(caption) {
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .table-scroll :global(th),
  .table-scroll :global(td) {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grid);
    text-align: right;
  }

  .table-scroll :global(thead th) {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-weight: 500;
    vertical-align: bottom;
    white-space: normal;
    min-width: 5.5rem;
  }

  .table-scroll :global(tbody th) {
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .notes {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .notes p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .notes strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .explorer :global(.load-error) {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .tiles {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .controls {
      padding: 0.75rem;
    }

    .control,
    .control select,
    #pick-district {
      width: 100%;
      min-width: 0;
    }

    .tiles :global(.tile-value) {
      font-size: 1.3rem;
    }

    .tooltip :global(.tip-label) {
      white-space: normal;
    }
  }
</style>
